From: Omarchy Mobile <omamobile@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom-smbchg: take the recharge threshold from the battery

smbchg_init() always sets the recharge threshold to 100 mV below the
float voltage. A battery that has just terminated relaxes by about that
much on its own, so on a phone left on the charger at full the charger
restarts within a minute, tops up for a few seconds, terminates again,
and so on: the status and the charge LED flicker between Full and
Charging, and the battery is held at the very top of its charge.

The charger also offers 200 mV. The battery's re-charge-voltage-microvolt
(charge_restart_voltage_uv) says where charging should restart; take
200 mV when that is at least 200 mV below voltage-max-design-microvolt,
and keep 100 mV otherwise, as before.

---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom-smbchg.c |   17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom-smbchg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom-smbchg.c
@@ -1467,7 +1467,7 @@
  */
 static int smbchg_init(struct smbchg_chip *chip)
 {
-	unsigned int value;
+	unsigned int value, rchg;
 	int ret;
 
 	/*
@@ -1524,10 +1524,21 @@
 		msleep(200);
 	}
 
-	/* Set recharge threshold to 100mV */
+	/*
+	 * Set the recharge threshold. The charger restarts charging either
+	 * 100 mV or 200 mV below the float voltage: take 200 mV when the
+	 * battery's re-charge voltage is at least that far below it, so that
+	 * a full battery left on the charger isn't topped up every minute.
+	 */
+	rchg = RCHG_THRESH_100MV;
+	if (chip->batt_info->charge_restart_voltage_uv > 0 &&
+	    chip->batt_info->voltage_max_design_uv > 0 &&
+	    chip->batt_info->voltage_max_design_uv -
+	    chip->batt_info->charge_restart_voltage_uv >= 200000)
+		rchg = RCHG_THRESH_200MV;
 	ret = qcom_pmic_sec_masked_write(chip->regmap,
 					 chip->base + SMBCHG_CHGR_CFG,
-					 RCHG_LVL_BIT, RCHG_THRESH_100MV);
+					 RCHG_LVL_BIT, rchg);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
